RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook00Page001Cue0001.Text:
{n}As Storyteller returns the scale to your hand, something goes wrong. First you notice your vision going black, but you quickly realize that it isn't just your vision, all of your senses are gone. Silence and darkness, these are the only accompaniments to your thoughts.{/n}
{n}Time seems to lose all meaning in the endless darkness that surrounds you. It is impossible to tell whether you've been here for minutes, hours, or days as the emptiness seems to stretch out to infinity. And then the silence is broken.{/n}
"Please stop, I don't know who you are or why you are doing this, but I can't take this anymore..." {n}In this endless darkness, you can't tell where the voice came from, but soon you hear the speaker once more as she screams out in pain. And then silence falls once again.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook01EndCue0002.Text:
"I wish I could say that I will follow you out of here and escape, but if you used my scale to reach here then it sounds like you are projecting your consciousness to my location rather than physically traveling here, so I doubt I can follow you when you leave. Could you please return to speak to me on occasion? I swear that I won't lose to this darkness. Just like you didn't lose to that wound."
{n}A gasp echoes in the darkness.{/n} "Wait, I do remember you, {name}. I met you before my fight against Deskari. You had an unnatural wound from a demonic attack. Why did I suddenly remember that? Could it be that talking to you is helping me to piece my memories together? If so, I hope to see you again, so we can have some more conversations."
{n}You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook03Page001Cue0001.Text:
{n}Focusing your energy into the scale again, you feel your surroundings shifting once more. As you open your eyes, you find yourself not in the wilderness of your last visit, but in a city under an open nighttime sky. Slowly a realization dawns on you as you take in your surroundings. This city is Kenabres, but you can tell that something is wrong. There is no damage from Deskari's attack. Rather, the city looks practically pristine. And perhaps more unsettling, there is no one around. There are no guards shuffling about on night patrol, no sounds of revelry from nearby taverns open late into the night, and no drunks stumbling on their way home. Just...{/n}{n}
silence.{/n}
{n} As you begin to contemplate the possible implications, the silence is finally broken as you hear the flapping of draconic wings from overhead. The silver dragon illuminated by the moonlight lands nearby before transforming into the familiar form of Terendelev to approach you.{/n} "I knew it would be only a matter of time before you would arrive {name}. Whatever happened here is too big for the Crusade to ignore."

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook03EndCue0005.Text:
"You changed the timeline? But why would I remember the original timeline then? If this was a ploy, then the mastermind wouldn't make that mistake. Couldn't make that mistake!" {n}Her eyes widen as a realization hits her.{/n} "You said that you communicate with me via one of my scales. I assume you had it on you when you traveled through time? Then I think I have an idea of what is happening."
{n}As she takes a moment to compose herself, the black fog ceases its advance, and begins to thin.{/n}
"I think my soul was sundered. Probably by that darkness that you found me in. I think you unintentionally dragged what was left of my soul and bound it to my scale. My memory has been shattered because a part of my soul is still in that darkness. I remember the original timeline because you unintentionally carried this portion of my soul with you when you changed history."
{n}She lets out a deep breath as the dark fog completely vanishes behind her.{/n} "I'm going to need to spend some time thinking about this, but thank you for not giving up on me. I don't know if there is any way to fix this, but hopefully we can find one." {n}She gives you a soft smile as you feel yourself returning to reality. You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook03EndCue0006.Text:
"I feel like the common thread in these discussions is that I'm missing memories where I would have reason to feel fear, doubt, and other negative emotions. So I only have Terendelev's positive emotions and memories? But then what happened to her... my? Negative memories?"
{n}As she takes a moment to compose herself, the black fog ceases its advance, and begins to thin.{/n}
"I think my soul was sundered. Probably by that darkness that you found me in. I think you unintentionally dragged what was left of my soul and bound it to my scale. My memory has been shattered because a part of my soul is still in that darkness."
{n}She lets out a deep breath as the dark fog completely vanishes behind her.{/n} "I'm going to need to spend some time thinking about this, but thank you for not giving up on me. I don't know if there is any way to fix this, but hopefully we can find one." {n}She gives you a soft smile as you feel yourself returning to reality. You open your eyes and find yourself back where you started holding the silver scale.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook04Page001Cue0001.Text:
{n}You stare at the draconic skull that was trying to kill you just moments ago. The missing vertebrae in the skeleton makes it clear that this was Terendelev's body reanimated by the demons. As you begin to ponder what this means for the Terendelev that you have come to know, you feel your senses beginning to fade away. You briefly notice the scale shining brightly before your surroundings completely disappear.{/n}
{n}As you regain your senses, you recognize your surroundings. You are in Kenabres again, but it is no longer the peaceful Kenabres of the last time you used the scale. Now it is the Kenabres on the day the demons invaded. Walls are destroyed, buildings are on fire, and you can see a pool of blood in the place where Deskari cut off Terendelev's head.{/n}
{n}Circling in the sky and occasionally roaring is the Ravener made of Terendelev's body. As you are looking around, you spot Terendelev in her human form nearby motioning for you to get over as she takes cover behind the remnants of a collapsed wall. She speaks as you join her behind cover.{/n} "So I have good news and bad news. Good news, my memory seems to be restoring itself. Bad news..." {n}She waves her arm towards the sky that is choked by smoke.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBook04EndCue0006.Text:
{n}Ignoring the Ravener, you turn your attention solely to Terendelev. You call upon your mastery over death. The magic that bound Terendelev to her scale is rudimentary at best, an accident caused by the mixture of multiple spells. You overwrite the magic with a proper binding spell. As the magic becomes set, chains spring out from the ground grabbing Terendelev's limbs. She turns to you and glares.{/n} "You're a monster. This goes against the natural order! There is no difference between you and the demons."
{n}Unable to move her arms, she spits at your feet.{/n} "I don't know what you think you are going to accomplish, but I refuse to cooperate." {n}The chains drag her down below the ground as the magic finishes binding her.{/n}
{n}You look up to the Ravener in the sky. With Terendelev properly bound and unable to be stolen from you, the ravener seems to have lost interest. The skeletal dragon redirects itself out of the city ruins, perhaps fleeing to the River of Souls. You open your eyes to see yourself back in Iz.{/n}

RANROMANCE_LOCALIZATION.RanRomTereBookFailEndCue0002.Text:
{n}You focus your mythic power into the scale. Almost as soon as you begin channeling the energy, you find yourself robbed of your senses again. The endless darkness surrounds you once more. You attempt to begin your search for the voice, but it is impossible to tell if you are even moving without any senses.{/n}
{n}As you ponder how to proceed, an idea occurs to you. If mythic power brought you here, perhaps it can help you as well. And so you bring your power to bear. There is no immediate change in your sight, but you can slowly feel your other senses returning for the darkness surrounding you has been dyed in your power. As you begin to gain your bearings, you hear a sob as a voice cries out.{/n} "No, not more darkness! Get away!"
{n}You blink as you find yourself back in reality. You look down to find that the scale has darkened and shattered. You briefly try and focus on the remnants before determining that the scale no longer works.{/n}

